# aegis/frr runtime pin
#
# The image aegis/frr:latest must resolve to. install.sh loads the shipped
# tarball, then VERIFIES the resulting image id equals this value. If it does
# not, install fails loudly — no silent stale substrate, no hand steps.
#
# RE-PINNED 2026-10-30 (Dad's call). The 2026-09-19 record below describes a
# DIFFERENT Dockerfile than the one in this tree and is retained, not deleted,
# because it is a true record of that date. Read the two sections separately.
#
# Produced 2026-09-19 (Cirrus-Nexus step 4 transport decision).
# Transport = image tarball, because the image is local-only (RepoDigests: []).
# This pin is the image ID read off a RUNNING container via docker inspect,
# NOT a build log.

# NOTE: image_id below is the DAEMON-LOCAL id on the build host. It is NOT the
# verification key: `docker save | docker load` recomputes the config digest on
# the target daemon, so the id changes across transport even for identical
# content. install.sh verifies on dockerfile_sha256 + layers_sha256 instead.
image_id=sha256:acb8d8dcd72a44c3389184bc168ee61444072566afaa59704eb1aa27250027b8
# Content-addressed rootfs layer chain (sha256 over the ordered layer digests).
# Transport-invariant: identical after save/load. THE identity key.
layers_sha256=bb7ef23a07dcb6c6b34e225dd77fa2eb592700975843ad1f1aa0105f49f9220c
dockerfile_sha256=cce15a8696ae045e8001f2b32107b1261fa7fc5ba30ad4cab5dfa8c7bc8f38cf
tarball=aegis-frr-image.tar.gz
tarball_sha256=9c6837d26d8dfb4bbbab62288cbb9f6528a48fd40b9e859b0cd7f4ecb43a1ff3
built=2026-09-19T16:01:57-04:00

# --- Re-pin, 2026-10-30 -----------------------------------------------------
#
# What actually happened, measured, not assumed:
#   The 2026-09-19 pin was built from Dockerfile.frr @ 2868142 (sha256 cce15a86...).
#   The NEXT DAY, 2026-09-20, commit 0503bc5 rewrote the daemon block: the old
#   sed matched nothing on FRR 10.x and silently no-op'd, so the build asserted
#   nothing at all. The rewrite writes the state and FAILS THE BUILD unless
#   ospfd=no and bgpd=no hold. Dockerfile.frr has been b3046a70... ever since.
#
#   So the pin never described anything this repo shipped -- the tarball it
#   names (aegis-frr-image.tar.gz) is in no commit and no tree, for either
#   version. A tarball restore path that can never be taken is not transport,
#   it is a hazard: it makes install.sh look like it verifies an image when it
#   has never once loaded one.
#
# Why this re-pin has no image_id / layers_sha256 / tarball_sha256:
#   I cannot measure them, so I will not write them. Producing them needs a
#   Docker daemon and a build; there is no working daemon on the host I run on
#   (`docker info` fails), and inventing a digest would be exactly the kind of
#   record this project keeps catching itself writing. The verifiable facts are
#   below; the image facts are marked UNPINNED until someone builds.
#
# What install.sh does with this file, unchanged and correct:
#   Step 7 stamps the real source hash into the image as the label
#   `aegis.frr.dockerfile.sha256` and rebuilds whenever it differs. THAT is the
#   live stale-substrate defence, and it needs no pin at all. This file is a
#   record of intent, not the verification key.

repin=2026-10-30
dockerfile_sha256=b3046a7027b7b6300e4babd596eae45f8820036a65aab5ad9c960e4ae9b7c39b
dockerfile_commit=0503bc5
dockerfile_commit_date=2026-09-20
tarball=
image_id=UNPINNED
layers_sha256=UNPINNED
tarball_sha256=UNPINNED
built=UNPINNED
